{"profile":{"name":"Rachel Chernos Lin","ward":"Ward 15, Don Valley West","bio":"Rachel Chernos Lin won the Ward 15 by-election on November 4, 2024, succeeding the late Jaye Robinson. She previously served as a Toronto District School Board trustee for six years (2018-2024), including two years as TDSB Chair. She holds an Honours BA from the University of Toronto and a Master's degree in History from Brown University, and is a published historian.","committees":["City-School Boards Advisory Committee (Chair)","Infrastructure and Environment Committee","Film, Television and Digital Media Advisory Board","North York Community Council","Toronto Hydro Corporation Board of Directors","Association of Municipalities of Ontario Board of Directors","Leaside Memorial Community Gardens Arena Board of Directors","Canadian Film Centre Board of Directors"],"contact":{"email":"Councillor_ChernosLin@toronto.ca","phone":"416-395-6408"},"promises":[{"text":"Manage development responsibly so neighbourhoods stay liveable, push for unit sizes that suit residents, and advocate for more affordable housing near transit plus complete communities with parks, recreation, and local childcare.","source":"https://www.voterachel.ca/priorities"},{"text":"Fight gridlock with a multi-pronged approach: modern signal technology, fewer long-term lane closures by developers, traffic monitors, safer and more efficient transit, and pedestrian safety under Vision Zero.","source":"https://www.voterachel.ca/priorities"},{"text":"Strengthen community safety by addressing home invasions, auto theft and gun violence, and supporting the five-year plan to hire 500 additional police officers while bringing down response times.","source":"https://www.voterachel.ca/priorities"}]},"lobbying":{"total":104,"term":104,"first":"2024-11-11","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":29,"clients":31,"subjects":56,"methods":{"Meetings":39,"Emails":57,"Phone calls":7,"Written":1,"Other or unreported":0},"top":[{"label":"Planning and De